WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
Drone operations depend on command, telemetry, video, and navigation signals.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.730
Urban radio congestion, metal structures, power infrastructure, terrain, foliage,

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:13.165
and the aircraft's orientation can reduce link quality or create intermittent behavior.

00:00:13.165 --> 00:00:16.520
Satellite-navigation performance depends on sky visibility, satellite geometry,

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.120
receiver condition, and reflected signals.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.590
Urban canyons and large surfaces can create multipath,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:24.240
where delayed reflections distort position.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.717
Compass sensors can also be affected by nearby metal or electrical fields.

00:00:27.717 --> 00:00:31.780
Check the launch area for interference and avoid calibrating or launching near vehicles,

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.900
reinforced structures, large metal objects,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.920
or energized equipment when guidance warns against it.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.035
Move to a safer area rather than normalizing unexplained alerts.

00:00:40.035 --> 00:00:42.830
Loss-of-signal planning must be completed before flight.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:46.130
Understand the aircraft's configured response, home-point status, route,

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.470
altitude assumptions, terrain, and obstacles.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:52.490
The correct response differs by site and must fit current official and manufacturer

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:53.189
guidance.

00:00:53.189 --> 00:00:56.600
Return-to-home is an automated contingency, not a universal rescue.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.455
An incorrect home point, unsuitable return altitude, changed recovery area,

00:01:00.455 --> 00:01:05.120
degraded navigation, or obstacle outside sensor capability can create new risk.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:08.000
Monitor signal trends and navigation behavior during flight.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.750
Recover early when quality degrades or position becomes unreliable.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.000
Do not continue deeper into a weak-link area because control has not yet been lost.
